# Grip Workflow Consolidation

**Canonical plugin:** `twintack-custom-grips` — team dashboard, My Custom Grips, statuses, mockups, messaging.

**Retired (remove, do not extend):** Gravity Forms, Make.com, Monday.com.

## Rules

1. New grip workflow features go in **twintack-custom-grips**, not Grip Manager or theme `functions.php`
2. Do not add Make.com webhook URLs, Monday REST endpoints, or `gform_*` hooks
3. `_grip_artwork_status` is the single source of truth for production stage — see `plugins/twintack-custom-grips/WORKFLOW.md`
4. Grip Manager is **legacy infrastructure** until merged — safe to remove Monday/Make code; keep CPT + WC sync until Phase 3
5. Historical `_grip_monday_*` meta: do not delete from DB; stop displaying in new UI

